arguments.content:
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: network-peer name resolution shadows local identities in `agent_message`**

`_resolveFabricAddress` now resolves network-DM peers **before** every local identity (`lib/src/task/subagent_tools.dart:1026-1031`):

```dart
final (networkTarget, networkError) = _resolveNetworkDmPeerAddress(
  manager,
  to,
);
if (networkError != null) return (to, networkError);
if (networkTarget != null) return (networkTarget, null);
// ...only AFTER this: selfId/"main", local handles, child names, fabric directory
```

`_resolveNetworkDmPeerAddress` matches a peer by **exact id** (safe — `network-dm-N` is synthetic) but then by **exact display name**. Peer names come from the remote side — the DM envelope `fromName` / roster label (`agent_cli_inbox.dart:123`, `agent_cli_network.dart:49`) — so a remote peer can label itself `"main"`, or the display name of an existing local sibling or fabric session. When that happens, `agent_message(to: "main")` (the documented parent keyword) or a name-addressed steer that used to reach the local mailbox is **silently delivered to the remote peer** over the encrypted transport — no error, no ambiguity prompt. The fail-closed ambiguity check covers network-vs-network duplicates only (`test/task/subagent_tools_test.dart` asserts `${peer.id}, ${duplicate.id}`), not network-vs-local collisions.

Suggested fix (keep the alias win, close the shadow):

```dart
// 1. exact network-peer id (synthetic namespace) — keep as-is
// 2. resolve local identities first: selfId, local handles, child names,
//    fabric directory names
// 3. fall through to network-peer NAME match only when no local identity
//    claimed the string — or include the matched local identity in the
//    ambiguity error so the model picks an id
```

Repro sketch: register a peer named `main` (or a name equal to a child handle), then call `agent_message(to: "main")` — it routes to the peer address instead of `manager.selfId`. A test asserting `to: "main"` still reaches the parent (and that a peer named like a local sibling fails closed with usable ids) would pin the contract.

